# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 1: METADATA BLOCK
# ( Identity, Provenance, VCS Exclusion Contracts & System Anchors )
# ==============================================================================
# @project       FaithNet
# @file          .gitignore
# @id            vcs.hygiene.gitignore
# @layer         Layer 0: Version Control & Workspace Hygiene Infrastructure
# @archetype     manifest | stateless
# @version       0.1.0-dev
# @interface_rev Rev 5
# @date          2026-11-17
# @updated       2026-11-17
# @author        CreativeWorkzStudio LLC / ProfessorSeanEX
# @repository    https://github.com/CreativeWorkzStudio/FaithNet
# @system        Git Version Control Invariant Exclusion Engine
# @role          Workspace Boundary Guard & Clean Tree Governance Manifest
# @maturity      Rev 5 Baseline | Wave 0 Genesis
# @chassis       stateless | Pure VCS boundary specification
# @scale         O(1) path filter across Go, AsciiDoc & multi-OS toolchains
# @seams         in: git working tree | exports: clean VCS staging boundary
# @invariants    1. Zero binary tracking: No compiled Go executables or objects.
#                2. Zero socket leakage: Transient IPC/Unix sockets stay local.
#                3. Zero telemetry leakage: Diagnostic runtime logs stay out.
#                4. Zero user-environment leakage: IDE & OS caches stay out.
#                5. Strict 80-column line width discipline across all lines.
#
# PURPOSE & ARCHITECTURAL ROLE:
#   Repository version control exclusion manifest and root hygiene guard for
#   FaithNet. Guarantees that compiled Go binaries, transient IPC sockets,
#   IDE workspace states, diagnostic dumps, coverage profiles, and OS cache
#   detritus never pollute Git history or corrupt cross-platform builds.
#
#   ### For Architects, Operators & Non-Programmers:
#   Keeps the FaithNet repository clean, portable, and free of temporary files
#   generated when running nodes, tests, or documentation compilers on Windows,
#   Linux, or macOS.
#
#   ### For Systems Programmers & Engine Architects:
#   Enforces clean VCS boundaries across Go build caches, test binaries,
#   pprof artifacts, Unix domain sockets, and AsciiDoc scratch intermediates.
#
# PEDAGOGICAL MISSION & THE BATON-PASSING LIFECYCLE:
#   This file models the Universal 5-Block Lifecycle Protocol:
#   - Block 1 (Metadata): Anchors identity, provenance, and hygiene contracts.
#   - Block 2 (Opening/Objects): Declares compiled binary and object artifacts.
#   - Block 3 (Body/Procedure): Filters build, socket, and doc intermediates.
#   - Block 4 (Audit/Telemetry): Filters logs, profiles, and test scratchpads.
#   - Block 5 (Closing/Teardown): Seals against OS and editor state detritus.
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 2: OPENING / COMPILED BINARIES BLOCK
# ( The Functional Objects: Declaring Machine Artifacts Prior to Execution )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.binaries
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 2.1: COMPILED GO EXECUTABLES & INTERMEDIATE OBJECTS ]
# Mission: Insulate the repository from platform-dependent compiled binaries.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Compiled Go executables, test binaries, and platform bundles
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib

# FaithNet CLI executables built at repository root
/faithnet-ping
/faithnet-node

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 2.2: BUILD & DISTRIBUTION STAGING DIRECTORIES ]
# Mission: Prevent local build staging trees from entering version control.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/bin/
/build/
build-*/
out/
dist/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 3: BODY / RUNTIME TRANSPORTS & DOC PIPELINE BLOCK
# ( The Procedural Logic: Runtime Socket, Radio & Doc Intermediates )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.runtime
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 3.1: TRANSIENT IPC SOCKETS & AUDIO/SERIAL DUMPS ]
# Mission: Keep ephemeral Rung 1/2 runtime transport artifacts local to host.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local Unix domain sockets and named pipes (transport/rung2_host/ipc.go)
*.sock
*.pipe

# Temporary raw PCM audio captures from Rung 1 AFSK tests
*.pcm
*.wav

# Local TLS private keys, sovereign Root CA directories & rollout PEMs
*.key
*.pem
.faithnet-certs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 3.2: DOCUMENTATION TOOLCHAIN TEMPORARY ARTIFACTS ]
# Mission: Prevent transient Asciidoctor and PDF compile intermediates.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.tmp
*.temp
.asciidoctor/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 4: AUDIT PROCEDURES, LOGS & TELEMETRY BLOCK
# ( The Audit Track: Forensic Telemetry, Profiles & Scratch Verification )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.telemetry
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 4.1: DIAGNOSTIC LOGS & PROFILING DUMPS ]
# Mission: Filter diagnostic logs, Go pprof captures, and coverage files.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.log
*.log.*
*.audit
*.telemetry
coverage.txt
coverage.out
cpu.prof
mem.prof

# Dedicated telemetry and log archives
logs/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 4.2: SCRATCHPADS & TEST HARNESS WORKING DIRECTORIES ]
# Mission: Isolate non-canonical experimental scripts and test outputs.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

scratch/
test_output/
debug_dumps/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 5: CLOSING / WORKSPACES & OS TEARDOWN BLOCK
# ( The Closing Handshake: Sealing Against IDE, Editor & OS State Detritus )
# Stratum: Version Control | Machine: vcs.hygiene.workspaces
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 5.1: IDE WORKSPACES & LANGUAGE SERVER CACHES ]
# Mission: Protect repository hygiene from developer-specific editor state.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.vscode/*
!.vscode/*.json
.idea/
.cache/

# Vim / Emacs swap buffers, lockfiles, and backup files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 5.2: OPERATING SYSTEM FILESYSTEM DETRITUS ]
# Mission: Guard against platform-specific desktop indexes and thumbnail stores.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# macOS metadata and desktop index files
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Windows desktop databases and thumbnail caches
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Linux filesystem metadata
.directory

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ SUB-ASSEMBLY 5.3: PATCH & MERGE REJECT ARTIFACTS ]
# Mission: Prevent local patch rejects and backup artifacts from entering tree.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.patch
*.orig
*.rej

# End of .gitignore
